_mutations(... outbound_mapper=PassthroughOutbound())` at :176, which routes through the unconditional threading path","outbound_mutation_builders.py:92 passes `status_map=status_map` unconditionally into `map_local_to_remote`; :249 passes `status_map=_status_map` unconditionally into `compute_update_fields` — the priority analog will likewise be unconditional, so doubles lacking the param raise TypeError"],"finding":"Threading a new unconditional `priority_map=` kwarg into `map_local_to_remote` / `map_fields_to_remote` / `compute_update_fields` (mirroring the unconditional `status_map=` threading at outbound_mutation_builders.py:87-92 and :236-250) will break existing TEST-DOUBLE implementations of these Protocol methods that have explicit signatures without `**kwargs` and do not accept `priority_map`; the plan's Scope and Testing sections enumerate only new fixtures, not updates to these existing doubles.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3b70123f3ab89d1e","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan sections 'Scope — every status_map carrier gains+forwards priority_map' and 'Testing'","norm_id":"n840525d5465afa7d","priority":0.7556,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running the existing outbound-differ / backend-neutrality / canonical-equivalence unit tests after the change, where the real differ threads priority_map into a test double that does not accept it"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add these test-double signature updates to the Scope/edit set (or accept `**kwargs` in them), exactly as the S2 status_map rollout must have done.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8889,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_